    "jsonld": "{\n  \"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n  \"@graph\": [\n    {\n      \"@type\": \"FAQPage\",\n      \"mainEntity\": [\n        {\n          \"@type\": \"Question\",\n          \"name\": \"Can Quickler use my own report template?\",\n          \"acceptedAnswer\": {\n            \"@type\": \"Answer\",\n            \"text\": \"Yes, and this is the main difference from other inspection software. Upload the finished report your firm already sends to clients, in Word or PDF, or even a photograph of one. Every record comes back inside that document with your styles, headings, tables, headers, footer and logo preserved. Quickler reads a finished report rather than a blank form, so it can separate your firm's standing wording from one visit's facts and place each record's words where yours were. Other tools give you their layout and you rebuild yours at the desk afterwards.\"\n          }\n        },\n        {\n          \"@type\": \"Question\",\n          \"name\": \"How much does Quickler cost?\",\n          \"acceptedAnswer\": {\n            \"@type\": \"Answer\",\n            \"text\": \"£75 per month per phone number & unlimited free dashboard accounts. Reports, the dashboard, sharing and downloads are free for everyone else, so you can add your whole team. A 30-person team with 5 regular inspectors pays £375 a month, against £570 to £720 on per-seat pricing at £19 to £24 a seat. Start with a 14-day free trial. Everything is unlocked and you need no card to start. Billed monthly in arrears by UK Direct Debit.\"\n          }\n        },\n        {\n          \"@type\": \"Question\",\n          \"name\": \"Is Quickler cheaper than iAuditor or SafetyCulture?\",\n          \"acceptedAnswer\": {\n            \"@type\": \"Answer\",\n            \"text\": \"It depends on the shape of your team, and we will be straight about it. Per-seat tools charge for every person on the licence whether they inspect daily or never open the app, so Quickler is substantially cheaper wherever a whole team needs access but only a handful do the walking: a care home, a school estate, a cleaning firm. If nearly everyone on your team inspects most days, for example five people all doing daily checks, a per-seat app will be cheaper than us.\"\n          }\n        },\n        {\n          \"@type\": \"Question\",\n          \"name\": \"Does my team need to install a new app?\",\n          \"acceptedAnswer\": {\n            \"@type\": \"Answer\",\n            \"text\": \"No. They answer in the WhatsApp already on their phone, or Telegram if you prefer, chosen per person. There is no new app to install, no login to remember and very little to learn. The usual reason inspection software quietly fails is that the people on site stop opening the app; Quickler removes that failure mode entirely. Only the manager signs in to the dashboard, with a magic link, a six-digit code or a passkey.\"\n          }\n        },\n        {\n          \"@type\": \"Question\",\n          \"name\": \"Can Quickler handle a long assessment, not just a short checklist?\",\n          \"acceptedAnswer\": {\n            \"@type\": \"Answer\",\n            \"text\": \"Yes. A live fire risk assessment check runs to over 380 questions, nested up to seven levels deep where the detail needs it. A single record holds up to 250 photos and 50 documents. There are thirteen question types: yes/no, written answer, number, date, time, photo, signature, graded word scales, location, weather, options, voice, and repeating tables for a row per item.\"\n          }\n        },\n        {\n          \"@type\": \"Question\",\n          \"name\": \"Does Quickler make things up or guess answers?\",\n          \"acceptedAnswer\": {\n            \"@type\": \"Answer\",\n            \"text\": \"No, and this is enforced rather than hoped for. Every name, number and identifier written on a record has to stand in something actually said, sent or photographed. Where two answers disagree, or a date reads two ways, Quickler raises it for a person to settle, quoting the words it heard and when they were said, rather than quietly choosing one. A plan to fix something is kept as a note, never recorded as the answer. A record never files itself just because every question happens to have been answered: somebody says done, or it waits.\"\n          }\n        },\n        {\n          \"@type\": \"Question\",\n          \"name\": \"What happens if there is no phone signal on site?\",\n          \"acceptedAnswer\": {\n            \"@type\": \"Answer\",\n            \"text\": \"WhatsApp holds the messages and delivers them when signal returns. Twenty messages arriving at once in the wrong order after a basement or a rural site is handled as one walk, not twenty fragments. Voice notes recorded in poor conditions are transcribed with the vocabulary of your trade taught to the transcriber, so the words specific to your job come out right.\"\n          }\n        },\n        {\n          \"@type\": \"Question\",\n          \"name\": \"What file formats can Quickler read and produce?\",\n          \"acceptedAnswer\": {\n            \"@type\": \"Answer\",\n            \"text\": \"It builds your check from Word, PDF, Excel, OpenDocument, plain text or a photograph of a paper form. A scanned PDF with no text layer is read as a picture rather than rejected. During a walk it accepts text, voice notes, photos, documents and a location pin. It produces your own report template filled in as Word or PDF, plus a shareable web page, PDF, Word, Excel, CSV and bulk zip downloads, all self-serve and available any time.\"\n          }\n        },\n        {\n          \"@type\": \"Question\",\n          \"name\": \"Is Quickler a care records system or an eMAR?\",\n          \"acceptedAnswer\": {\n            \"@type\": \"Answer\",\n            \"text\": \"No. Quickler is the audit and evidence layer, not a clinical or care records system. It does not hold care plans, medication rounds, resident records or rostering, and those stay in your care planning system, which remains the single source of truth. It records that a check was done and keeps the evidence with it. It is also not job management software: no scheduling of work, no invoicing, no dispatch.\"\n          }\n        },\n        {\n          \"@type\": \"Question\",\n          \"name\": \"Who is Quickler for?\",\n          \"acceptedAnswer\": {\n            \"@type\": \"Answer\",\n            \"text\": \"Any team that inspects, audits or keeps a record away from a desk: care homes and domiciliary care, nurseries and early years, schools, colleges and university estates, fire risk assessors, cleaning and facilities firms, health and safety consultants, field-services trades and fleet operators. It is a general system, so a firm builds whatever check shape it needs and the same engine runs all of them. UK-first, and it works anywhere WhatsApp does.\"\n          }\n        },\n        {\n          \"@type\": \"Question\",\n          \"name\": \"How long does it take to set up?\",\n          \"acceptedAnswer\": {\n            \"@type\": \"Answer\",\n            \"text\": \"Setup to a first live check typically takes under a week. You need a company name and the phone numbers of the people who will do the walks. If you upload the form or the finished report you already use, Quickler writes the questions from it, so most of the setup is done by the document you already have.\"\n          }\n        },\n        {\n          \"@type\": \"Question\",\n          \"name\": \"Where is the data stored and who can see it?\",\n          \"acceptedAnswer\": {\n            \"@type\": \"Answer\",\n            \"text\": \"On EU servers under a Data Processing Agreement with each customer. The customer is the controller and owns the data; Quickler is the processor. Admins see everything in the firm; the people doing the walks see only their own WhatsApp conversation and have no account. Every record carries a full edit history of who changed what and when. Quickler is registered with the Information Commissioner's Office, registration ZC124993. You can download everything yourself at any time, and on cancellation you download every record and Quickler deletes its copy.\"\n          }\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"@type\": \"ItemList\",\n      \"name\": \"quickler use case pages\",\n      \"itemListElement\": [\n        {\n          \"@type\": \"ListItem\",\n          \"position\": 1,\n          \"url\": \"https://quickler.co/pages/what-is-quickler.html\",\n          \"name\": \"What is quickler?\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"@type\": \"ListItem\",\n          \"position\": 2,\n          \"url\": \"https://quickler.co/pages/van-safety-checks.html\",\n          \"name\": \"WhatsApp Van Safety Checks\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"@type\": \"ListItem\",\n          \"position\": 3,\n          \"url\": \"https://quickler.co/pages/site-inspections.html\",\n          \"name\": \"WhatsApp Site Inspections\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"@type\": \"ListItem\",\n          \"position\": 4,\n          \"url\": \"https://quickler.co/pages/compliance-certificates.html\",\n          \"name\": \"WhatsApp Compliance Certificates\"\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}"
