    "html": "<p>Hello,</p><p>I am Philip, and I started Quickler.</p><p>If you carry out inspections for a living, you'll know the pain that comes after the site: the typing, the moving of photos, the formatting. The site is the valuable part, because that is where your competence is needed.</p><p>But then comes the desk. Muddled notes about things you noticed on the way out, photos you assumed you'd be able to work out later, bad handwriting, or a drop-down menu that forces you to say something not quite right.</p><p>Quickler solves all of this, in less than 20% of the time. Talk on WhatsApp as you go round. Send photos when you need to. Get reminded of what you haven't mentioned yet. Quickler puts each thing where it belongs, in your own layout. If you don't say something, we don't make it up. If you do, we don't lose it. It will even notice things you miss.</p><p>It won't be perfect. Sometimes a photo of the emergency lighting goes under escape lighting. But each time you correct it, you teach Quickler, like you would a new employee.</p><p>Quickler's <a href=\"/believe/\">principles are here</a>. <a href=\"https://app.quickler.co/signup\">Try it free for 14 days</a> and cut your desk time by 80%. If you get stuck, <a href=\"mailto:philipross@quickler.co\">email me</a>. I read every one.</p>",
